infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Alert severity split — RED pages, USE warns
  desc Alert user-facing symptoms (RED) at page-grade; alert internal causes (USE) at warning-grade. The single strongest lever against alert fatigue.
  compares
    - label RED → page the on-call human
      children
        - label Latency SLO breach
          desc p99 Duration > 200 ms for 5 min — the user already feels the slowness, so a human must respond now.
        - label Error rate spike
          desc Errors > 1% for 2 min — requests are failing in real time; page on-call.
        - label Trigger — user is already unhappy
          desc RED alerts wake humans because users are affected. Symptom before cause: this is what justifies interrupting someone's sleep.
    - label USE → notify Slack or a ticket
      children
        - label CPU saturation
          desc PSI cpu some > 20% for 10 min — resource pressure, not yet user pain. No need to page.
        - label Memory pressure
          desc PSI memory full > 0 for 5 min — capacity team plans ahead while on-call keeps sleeping.
        - label Disk headroom
          desc Disk > 90% for 5 min — plan capacity before it ever becomes a RED incident.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b
